meta {
  name: Close Room
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Close Room

  Owner-only, graceful close. If no round is live, the room closes
  immediately (`closed: true`); if a round is live, the room moves to
  `status: "closing"` (`closed: false`) and actually closes once that round
  settles — see `docs/GAME_RULES.md`.

  **Expected success**: `200` with `{room_id, status, closed, reason}`.

  **Expected errors**:
  - `401 unauthorized` — missing/invalid/expired bearer token.
  - `403 not_owner` — the caller (`{{token}}`) does not own `{{roomId}}`.
    Try swapping in `{{token2}}` to see this on purpose.
  - `404 room_not_found` — `{{roomId}}` doesn't exist (e.g. it was never
    set — run "Create Room" first).
  - `409 room_closed` — the room is already closed.
}
